    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0389" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg287"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4352: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-06T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 6,
                                1927—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Your 5, January 4, noon. Inform commander of Legation Guard of representations
                    made by British and Italian Chargés d’Affaires, and forward the text thereof to
                    the Department by next pouch.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d256-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d256-f1" n="7" xml:id="d256-f1-content">
                <p>Forwarded in despatch No. 332, Jan. 12, 1927 (not printed).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
